cloudevents-cpp provides CMake targets:

    find_package(cloudevents CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ce::core ce::format_json ce::binding_http)

The Protobuf format is a target of its own with no dependency beyond the core, so it needs
no feature:

    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ce::core ce::format_protobuf)

The default feature "nlohmann" adds the codec, which is a component:

    find_package(cloudevents CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS codec_nlohmann)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ce::codec_nlohmann)

Install with the "rapidjson" or "boost-json" feature for those codecs, or
without any codec by turning the default features off:

    vcpkg install "cloudevents-cpp[core]" --overlay-ports=<clone>/packaging/vcpkg/ports
